#var, use command >Rest Client: Switch Environment in search bar of vs code
@id =1

###

### Get all academic loads
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/academic-loads HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Get academic load by ID
GET http://localhost:3000/api/v1/academic-loads/{{id}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

###

### Create a new academic load
POST http://localhost:3000/api/v1/academic-loads HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nrc": "12345",
  "academicPeriodId": "6815575560d75b5b1c7f1c13",
  "campusId": "68155584c434b0977c70af87",
  "courseId": "681584d5dcb8cfd70156e071",
  "classroomId": "681557e260d75b5b1c7f1c15",
  "maximumCapacity": 30,
  "enrolledCapacity": 25,
  "availableSeats": 5,
  "groupId": "681557e260d75b5b1c7f1345",
  "scheduleId": "68158152dcb8cfd70156e06e",
  "professorId": "681572443c140c7aad19542d",
  "date": "2025-04-19T14:30:00Z",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### Update an existing academic load
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/v1/academic-loads/{{id}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "nrc": "12345",
  "maximumCapacity": 35,
  "enrolledCapacity": 28,
  "availableSeats": 7,
  "date": "2025-04-20T14:30:00Z",
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

###

### Delete an academic load
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/v1/academic-loads/{{id}} HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json